              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A reefer trailer, short for refrigerated trailer, is the unsung hero of the logistics world. These specialized trailers are designed to transport perishable goods like produce, dairy, meat, and pharmaceuticals safely across long distances. Unlike standard dry vans, reefer trailers use a refrigerated trailer system that keeps cargo within a specific temperature range, no matter the weather outside.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For fleet owners and independent operators, understanding how these systems work is essential. Proper operation and maintenance of a reefer trailer mean fewer spoiled loads, better fuel efficiency, and a stronger reputation for reliability, all factors that directly impact your bottom line.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-how-it-works",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How Does a Reefer Trailer Work?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "how-it-works"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-it-works-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At the core of every reefer trailer is a closed-loop refrigeration system made up of three key components:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-how-it-works-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type3",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Evaporator Coil",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Absorbs heat from inside the trailer."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Compressor",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Pressurizes refrigerant gas and moves it through the system."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Condenser Coil",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Expels heat outside the trailer."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-it-works-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When the reefer unit is powered on, the compressor circulates refrigerant through the coils. As warm air from the trailer passes over the evaporator, heat is absorbed and released outside via the condenser. This continuous cycle creates a controlled environment, keeping internal temperatures steady, often between -20°F and 70°F, depending on the load.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-it-works-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Modern reefer trailers are equipped with temperature control systems that allow drivers to set and monitor cargo conditions in real time. Some models even include data tracking and alerts that notify the operator if temperatures fluctuate, protecting valuable shipments before issues arise.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-how-it-works-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A significant share of food produced globally is lost or wasted somewhere in the supply chain each year. Ensuring your company has the right equipment to maintain consistent cooling makes a measurable difference in profitability and sustainability.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-does-a-reefer-trailer-work/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician performing a pre-trip inspection on a reefer trailer with a clipboard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-maintenance",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Reefer Trailer Maintenance: The Key to Reliable Cooling",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "maintenance"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-maintenance-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A reefer trailer is only as dependable as its maintenance schedule. Routine reefer trailer maintenance ensures your system runs efficiently and prevents costly downtime. We recommend focusing on:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-maintenance-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "<strong>Regular pre-trip inspections</strong> — check fuel levels, belts, hoses, and refrigerant before every haul"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "<strong>Cleaning evaporator and condenser coils</strong> — debris can restrict airflow and cause uneven cooling"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "<strong>Monitoring thermostats and sensors</strong> — faulty sensors can misread temperatures, leading to cargo spoilage"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "<strong>Routine oil changes and filter replacements</strong> — these small steps keep compressors running smoothly and extend system life"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-maintenance-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you operate in Florida's demanding climate, this maintenance becomes even more critical. High humidity and long hours on the road can strain your cooling unit. That's why Sun State Trailers offers reefer trailer repair and service across multiple locations, helping you stay on schedule and compliant with cold chain regulations.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "actions-maintenance-4",
                  "type": "buttons",
                  "props": {
                    "align": "left",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "ctaId": "browse-new-trailers",
                        "label": "New Trailers",
                        "style": "primary"
                      },
                      {
                        "ctaId": "browse-used-trailers",
                        "label": "Used Trailers",
                        "style": "secondary"
                      },
                      {
